  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Fire on the Mountain** (2 reviews, 1 other source): Also recommended as a highlight worth hearing on this recording; Reviewer says it is Ween playing it, Rev. B.ill singing, confirmed by a video the audio was taken from [2][4][5]\n- **Gabrielle** (1 review): Called the definitive version; Deaner and Rev. B.ill trade guitar licks like Thin Lizzy's guitarists [5]\n- **Band on the Run** (1 review): Singled out as a reason to download the recording: Ween's version of the song [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Allman Sunrise**: back after 67 archived shows (646 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [7]\n- **Band on the Run**: back after 67 archived shows (646 days) [7]\n- **Fire on the Mountain**: back after 62 archived shows (409 days); rare: 6 archived performances [7]\n- **raffle time**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Gabrielle [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Ween2000-06-10.unknown** (recommended): source not stated; 12 songs; 51 min [1]\n- **ween2000-06-10**: audience recording; 11 songs; 50 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [2]. Said about its sound: The taper did a good job capturing the sound of this audience recording [4]\n- **ween-2000-06-10-solebury-high**: source not stated; 0 songs; 58 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Outdoor daytime show on the Solebury High School soccer field, played from a trailer that opens at the side [1]\n- Says this is not the only time Ween has performed Fire on the Mountain [5]\n- Took place during Ween's short break between two heavy White Pepper tours in summer 2000 [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Ween2000-06-10.unknown**: Unknown audience source, through an unknown step to CDR, then EAC, then FLAC [1]\n- **ween2000-06-10**: taped by Unknown; transferred by Unknown; source: Unknown Aud (possibly video camera) [2]",
